WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:07.020
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar. This classic problem is making the rounds because it it easy to state

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.100
but evidently, it's extremely hard for adults to solve.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.520
Can you figure it out?

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:21.020
The problem is to make 3 squares of equal size by moving 3 of the sticks.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.600
The problem is like it sounds, there are no other tricks.

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.360
You are not allowed to break any of the sticks,

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:33.560
the 3 resulting squares must be of equal size,

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.080
and each stick in the resulting shape must be part of a square.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.460
Give the problem a try and when you're ready, keep watching the video for the solution

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:52.080
The only difficult part is selecting which sticks to move

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.560
Here is one possible solution

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.220
On our first move we will move this stick

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.920
This will be our second move

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.320
And this will be our third move

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.040
And what we have is a shape that has

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.520
Three squares of equal sides

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.360
Now due to the symmetry of the problem you could have also found this

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.520
by moving three other sticks

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.660
you may have also come up with the same shape upside down

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:28.660
But this is the basic solution

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.180
Did you figure it out?

